IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Telecommunications Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia), Part 19 -- statutory infrastructure providers, from the seat of the
-- person or business that wants premises connected: what counts as a qualifying (broadband) service (s 360A, s 360AA); who the
-- statutory infrastructure provider for my premises is (ss 360C, 360F, 360G, 360K, 360KA, 360KB, 360L); whether it must connect
-- my premises, to which kind of network, and on what request (s 360P(1), (2), (10)); how long it has to answer and what I am told
-- if it refuses (s 360P(11A), (12)); on what terms (s 360P(8), (9), s 360W(2), (4)); voice calls on the wholesale service
-- (s 360Q(1A), (1B)); notice if my area's provider will stop being able to serve it (ss 360R(2), (3), 360SA); and damages for a
-- breach of a designated compensable standard or rule, with the provider's deadlines (ss 360VD, 360VE).
--
-- SEAT: the end-user -- the person or business at premises who wants a broadband connection. "Am I entitled to be connected
-- to a network that can carry broadband? Who has to do it? What do I have to ask for, and through whom? How long can they take?
-- What if they refuse?" Part 19 is addressed to the provider and to carriage service providers (retailers); the duties are
-- encoded as regulative rules on them and as what they mean for the end-user. Every judgment the Part leaves to someone else
-- (whether a request is reasonable, whether a fixed-line connection is reasonable, whether a Ministerial determination applies)
-- is asked as an input, never guessed.
--
-- Edition: the compilation registered as C2026C00224 (Compilation No. 117, compilation date 4 June 2026, includes amendments
-- up to Act No. 75, 2025; Federal Register of Legislation, retrieved 13 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05145.txt. No instrument is deposited: every Ministerial
-- determination, standard, benchmark, rule and the compensation rules are asked as facts or left as inputs.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Parts 1-18 and 20 onwards; Division 2 machinery (how areas are declared, ss 360H-360J, 360LA-360NA, beyond
-- what the end-user can state about the area); s 360P(3A), (4)-(7), s 360Q(2)-(8) (Ministerial determinations and
-- requirements, asked as facts where the answer turns on them); s 360Q(9)-(13) (the wholesale request process, which is the
-- retailer's); s 360RA, s 360SB (rules not deposited); s 360S (targets for NBN Co, a statement of intent); s 360U, s 360V
-- (standards and rules, not deposited); s 360VF (Ombudsman certificates); s 360X; Division 6 onwards (information, audits,
-- reports, the register, delegation). What a standard, a benchmark or the compensation rules say is not encoded.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the end-user's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Telecommunications Act 1997, Part 19 -- the person or business wanting a connection`

§§ `The parties and their acts`

-- The parties Part 19 names, as they meet the end-user. "Carriage service provider" is the retailer the end-user deals with.
DECLARE `Telecom party` IS ONE OF
    `the statutory infrastructure provider`
    `my carriage service provider`
    `me, the end-user`

DECLARE `Answer to the request` IS ONE OF
    `will fulfil the request`
    `refuses the request`

DECLARE `Decision on liability` IS ONE OF
    `accepts the liability`
    `does not accept the liability`

DECLARE `Telecom act` IS ONE OF
    -- s 360P(1): the retailer's request "on behalf of an end-user at premises in the service area"
    `request connection of my premises`
    -- s 360P(11A)(a): "(i) notify the carriage service provider that the statutory infrastructure provider will fulfil the
    -- request; or (ii) refuse the request"
    `answer the request` HAS `the answer` IS AN `Answer to the request`
    -- s 360P(1)(a) or (b): connecting the premises to a qualifying telecommunications network
    `connect my premises`
    -- s 360P(12)(c): "give written notice of the refusal, and the reasons for the refusal, to the carriage service provider"
    `give my carriage service provider written notice of the refusal and the reasons`
    -- s 360P(12)(d): "give a copy of the notice to the end-user"
    `give me a copy of the refusal notice`
    -- s 360SA(2): "give written notice of the matter to each of those end-users"
    `give me written notice of the matter`
    -- s 360VE(1): "decide whether to accept that liability"
    `decide whether to accept liability for damages` HAS `the decision` IS A `Decision on liability`
    -- s 360VE(3): "give the customer written notification of the decision"
    `give me written notification that it does not accept liability`
    -- s 360VE(4), (5): discharging the liability, by a credit or another way
    `discharge the liability`

§§ `s 360A, s 360AA -- does this service count as broadband (a qualifying carriage service)`

-- s 360A: "qualifying carriage service means: (a) a qualifying fixed-line carriage service; or (b) a qualifying fixed wireless
-- carriage service; or (c) a qualifying satellite carriage service." Fixed-line: "(a) ... enables end-users to download
-- communications; and (b) ... supplied using a line to premises occupied or used by an end-user; and (c) the peak download
-- transmission speed ... is at least 25 megabits per second; and (d) the peak upload transmission speed ... is at least 5
-- megabits per second." Satellite: the same with "supplied using a satellite", "but does not include a public mobile
-- telecommunications service". s 360AA(1): fixed wireless: "(a) supplied using a fixed wireless technology platform; and (b)
-- ... marketed to customers, or potential customers, as a fixed wireless service; and (c)-(e)" the same download and speeds;
-- "(f) ... not a public mobile telecommunications service; and (g) ... a listed carriage service; and (h) the conditions (if
-- any) determined under subsection (2) are satisfied."
DECLARE `How the service reaches the premises` IS ONE OF
    `a line to the premises (such as fibre, copper or cable)`
    `a fixed wireless technology platform`
    `a satellite`
    `a public mobile network`

`the minimum peak download speed in megabits per second` MEANS 25
`the minimum peak upload speed in megabits per second` MEANS 5

@export Does this service count as broadband under Part 19 (a qualifying carriage service)?
GIVEN `how it reaches the premises` IS A `How the service reaches the premises` @desc How the service is delivered to the premises: a line (fibre, copper or cable), fixed wireless, satellite, or a mobile network
      `it lets me download` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service lets you download communications (for example web pages, video, files)
      `peak download speed` IS A NUMBER @desc The service's peak download speed, in megabits per second
      `peak upload speed` IS A NUMBER @desc The service's peak upload speed, in megabits per second
      `it is marketed as fixed wireless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For fixed wireless only: whether the service is marketed to customers as a fixed wireless service
      `it is a listed carriage service meeting any Ministerial conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For fixed wireless only: whether it is a listed carriage service and meets any conditions the Minister has determined under s 360AA(2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a qualifying carriage service` IF
        `it lets me download`
    AND `peak download speed` AT LEAST `the minimum peak download speed in megabits per second`
    AND `peak upload speed` AT LEAST `the minimum peak upload speed in megabits per second`
    AND (    `how it reaches the premises` EQUALS `a line to the premises (such as fibre, copper or cable)`
          OR `how it reaches the premises` EQUALS `a satellite`
          OR (    `how it reaches the premises` EQUALS `a fixed wireless technology platform`
              AND `it is marketed as fixed wireless`
              AND `it is a listed carriage service meeting any Ministerial conditions`))

§§ `ss 360C-360L -- who is the statutory infrastructure provider for my premises`

-- s 360C: four kinds of service area. s 360F(1): "the general service area means Australia, other than: (a) a nominated
-- service area; or (aa) a pending area ...; or (ab) an anticipated service area; or (b) a designated service area." s 360G:
-- "NBN Co is the statutory infrastructure provider for the general service area." s 360K: for a nominated service area, the
-- carrier or carriage service provider whose declaration made it, unless the Minister declares another (s 360K(1)-(2)).
-- s 360KA: an area in an anticipatory notice (ss 360HA, 360HC) is an anticipated service area once "(c) ... at least one of
-- those building units: (i) the construction of the building unit has been completed; (ii) the building unit is occupied",
-- and "(d) ... does not consist of, and is not included in" a nominated or designated service area. s 360KB: its provider is
-- the carrier or carriage service provider that gave the notice, unless the Minister declares another. s 360F(2): until then
-- the notice area is a "pending area", except premises where "NBN Co provides qualifying carriage services to end-users"
-- (s 360F(2)(c)); a pending area is in no service area. s 360L: a designated service area's provider is the one, or each of
-- the ones, the Minister declares. A designated area is excluded from a nominated one (s 360H(1)(b)). Which declarations and
-- notices exist is on the register (s 360Z) and is asked as fact.
DECLARE `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider` IS ONE OF
    `NBN Co: my premises are in the general service area (ss 360F, 360G)`
    `the carrier or carriage service provider the Minister declared for my designated service area; where there are several, any of them may meet the obligations (s 360L)`
    `the carrier or carriage service provider whose declaration made my nominated service area, unless the Minister has declared another (s 360K)`
    `the carrier or carriage service provider that gave the anticipatory notice for my anticipated service area, unless the Minister has declared another (ss 360KA, 360KB)`
    `none yet: my premises are in a pending area (an area named in an anticipatory notice where no building unit is yet completed and occupied), which is in no service area (s 360F(1)(aa), (2))`

@export Who is the statutory infrastructure provider that must connect my premises?
GIVEN `my premises are in a designated service area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your premises are in an area the Minister has declared a designated service area (s 360L)
      `my premises are in a nominated service area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your premises are in a nominated service area, usually a new development whose network a carrier or carriage service provider other than NBN Co installed and declared (ss 360H, 360HB, 360J)
      `my premises are in an area named in an anticipatory notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your premises are in an area named in a notice a carrier or carriage service provider gave the ACMA before installing a network for a development (ss 360HA, 360HC)
      `a building unit in that area is completed and occupied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether at least one building unit in that area has been completed and is occupied
      `NBN Co already provides qualifying services at my premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether NBN Co already provides broadband (qualifying carriage services) to an end-user at your premises
GIVETH A `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider`
DECIDE `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` IS
    IF `my premises are in a designated service area`
    THEN `the carrier or carriage service provider the Minister declared for my designated service area; where there are several, any of them may meet the obligations (s 360L)`
    ELSE IF `my premises are in a nominated service area`
         THEN `the carrier or carriage service provider whose declaration made my nominated service area, unless the Minister has declared another (s 360K)`
         ELSE IF `my premises are in an area named in an anticipatory notice` AND `a building unit in that area is completed and occupied`
              THEN `the carrier or carriage service provider that gave the anticipatory notice for my anticipated service area, unless the Minister has declared another (ss 360KA, 360KB)`
              ELSE IF `my premises are in an area named in an anticipatory notice` AND (NOT `NBN Co already provides qualifying services at my premises`)
                   THEN `none yet: my premises are in a pending area (an area named in an anticipatory notice where no building unit is yet completed and occupied), which is in no service area (s 360F(1)(aa), (2))`
                   ELSE `NBN Co: my premises are in the general service area (ss 360F, 360G)`

§§ `s 360P(1), (2), (10) -- am I entitled to be connected (if you want premises connected)`

-- s 360P(1): "The statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must, on reasonable request by a carriage service
-- provider on behalf of an end-user at premises in the service area: (a) connect the premises to a qualifying fixed-line
-- telecommunications network in order that the carriage service provider can provide qualifying fixed-line carriage services to
-- the end-user at the premises; or (b) if it is not reasonable for the statutory infrastructure provider to connect the
-- premises to a qualifying fixed-line telecommunications network--connect the premises to a qualifying telecommunications
-- network in order that the carriage service provider can provide: (i) qualifying fixed wireless carriage services ...; or (ii)
-- qualifying satellite carriage services". (2): "An obligation does not arise ... in the circumstances (if any) specified in a
-- determination under subsection (3)." (10): the Minister may determine when a fixed-line connection is "taken not to be
-- reasonable". The end-user cannot ask the provider directly: the request is the carriage service provider's.
DECLARE `Am I entitled to be connected` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the statutory infrastructure provider must connect my premises to a qualifying fixed-line network, so my retailer can supply me fixed-line broadband of at least 25/5 Mbps peak (s 360P(1)(a))`
    `yes: a fixed-line connection is not reasonable, so the statutory infrastructure provider must connect my premises to a network for qualifying fixed wireless or satellite broadband of at least 25/5 Mbps peak (s 360P(1)(b))`
    `not yet: the obligation arises only on a reasonable request by a carriage service provider on my behalf, so I must ask a retailer to make the request (s 360P(1))`
    `no: the request is not a reasonable request, so no obligation arises (s 360P(1))`
    `no: a Ministerial determination under s 360P(3) says no obligation arises in my circumstances (s 360P(2))`
    `no: my premises are in a pending area, which is in no service area, so there is no statutory infrastructure provider for them yet (s 360F(2))`

@export Am I entitled to have my premises connected to a network that can carry broadband, and to what kind?
GIVEN `my premises are in a designated service area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your premises are in an area the Minister has declared a designated service area (s 360L)
      `my premises are in a nominated service area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your premises are in a nominated service area (a development whose network a carrier or carriage service provider other than NBN Co installed and declared)
      `my premises are in an area named in an anticipatory notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your premises are in an area named in an anticipatory notice given to the ACMA for a development (ss 360HA, 360HC)
      `a building unit in that area is completed and occupied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether at least one building unit in that area has been completed and is occupied
      `NBN Co already provides qualifying services at my premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether NBN Co already provides broadband (qualifying carriage services) to an end-user at your premises
      `a carriage service provider has asked on my behalf` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a carriage service provider (a retailer such as the company you buy internet from) has asked the statutory infrastructure provider to connect your premises on your behalf
      `the request is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the request is a reasonable request (a judgment for the provider and, in a dispute, a court; answer as found or agreed)
      `a s 360P(3) determination excludes it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a determination by the Minister under s 360P(3) says no obligation arises in your circumstances
      `a fixed-line connection is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is reasonable for the provider to connect your premises to a fixed-line network (FALSE if a Ministerial determination under s 360P(10) says it is taken not to be reasonable for premises like yours)
GIVETH AN `Am I entitled to be connected`
DECIDE `Am I entitled to be connected question` IS
    IF `Who is my statutory infrastructure provider question` `my premises are in a designated service area` `my premises are in a nominated service area` `my premises are in an area named in an anticipatory notice` `a building unit in that area is completed and occupied` `NBN Co already provides qualifying services at my premises` EQUALS `none yet: my premises are in a pending area (an area named in an anticipatory notice where no building unit is yet completed and occupied), which is in no service area (s 360F(1)(aa), (2))`
    THEN `no: my premises are in a pending area, which is in no service area, so there is no statutory infrastructure provider for them yet (s 360F(2))`
    ELSE IF `a s 360P(3) determination excludes it`
         THEN `no: a Ministerial determination under s 360P(3) says no obligation arises in my circumstances (s 360P(2))`
         ELSE IF (NOT `a carriage service provider has asked on my behalf`)
              THEN `not yet: the obligation arises only on a reasonable request by a carriage service provider on my behalf, so I must ask a retailer to make the request (s 360P(1))`
              ELSE IF (NOT `the request is reasonable`)
                   THEN `no: the request is not a reasonable request, so no obligation arises (s 360P(1))`
                   ELSE IF `a fixed-line connection is reasonable`
                        THEN `yes: the statutory infrastructure provider must connect my premises to a qualifying fixed-line network, so my retailer can supply me fixed-line broadband of at least 25/5 Mbps peak (s 360P(1)(a))`
                        ELSE `yes: a fixed-line connection is not reasonable, so the statutory infrastructure provider must connect my premises to a network for qualifying fixed wireless or satellite broadband of at least 25/5 Mbps peak (s 360P(1)(b))`

§§ `s 360P(11A), (12) -- how long the provider has to answer, and what I am told if it refuses`

-- s 360P(11A): the provider "must: (i) notify the carriage service provider that the statutory infrastructure provider will
-- fulfil the request; or (ii) refuse the request; and (b) do so within: (i) 10 business days after receiving the request; or
-- (ii) if a longer period is specified under subsection (11B)--that longer period." (12): if it refuses, it "must: (i) give
-- written notice of the refusal, and the reasons for the refusal, to the carriage service provider; and (ii) do so within 5
-- business days after the refusal; and (d) if the carriage service provider receives the notice--the carriage service provider
-- must: (i) give a copy of the notice to the end-user; and (ii) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice."
-- Counted in business days. The connection itself must be made within the maximum period in the provider's published terms
-- (s 360W(2)), which is an input (no standard under s 360U(1)(f) is deposited).
`the business days to answer a connection request` MEANS 10
`the business days to give written notice of a refusal` MEANS 5
`the business days for my retailer to pass on the refusal notice` MEANS 5

GIVEN `a longer period specified by the Minister` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the period to answer` IS
    IF `a longer period specified by the Minister` GREATER THAN `the business days to answer a connection request`
    THEN `a longer period specified by the Minister`
    ELSE `the business days to answer a connection request`

-- The duty chain, as one regulative rule, on a business-day clock starting when the provider receives the request.
GIVEN `a longer period specified by the Minister` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum connection period in the published terms` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Telecom party` `Telecom act`
DECIDE `s 360P(1), (11A), (12) -- the provider must answer my retailer's request, connect me or give reasons, and my retailer must pass the reasons on` IS
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider`
    MUST  `answer the request` answer
    WITHIN `the period to answer` `a longer period specified by the Minister`
    HENCE
        IF answer EQUALS `refuses the request`
        THEN PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider`
             MUST  `give my carriage service provider written notice of the refusal and the reasons`
             WITHIN `the business days to give written notice of a refusal`
             HENCE
                 PARTY `my carriage service provider`
                 MUST  `give me a copy of the refusal notice`
                 WITHIN `the business days for my retailer to pass on the refusal notice`
                 LEST  BREACH BY `my carriage service provider` BECAUSE "s 360P(12)(d): the carriage service provider must give the end-user a copy of the refusal notice within 5 business days after receiving it"
             LEST  BREACH BY `the statutory infrastructure provider` BECAUSE "s 360P(12)(c): the provider must give written notice of the refusal and the reasons within 5 business days after the refusal"
        ELSE PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider`
             MUST  `connect my premises`
             WITHIN `the maximum connection period in the published terms`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the statutory infrastructure provider` BECAUSE "s 360P(1), (9), s 360W(2): the provider must connect the premises within the maximum period in its published terms"
    LEST  BREACH BY `the statutory infrastructure provider` BECAUSE "s 360P(11A): the provider must notify that it will fulfil the request, or refuse it, within 10 business days (or the longer period specified)"

@export How many business days does the provider have to tell my retailer whether it will connect me (s 360P(11A))?
GIVEN `a longer period specified by the Minister` IS A NUMBER @desc A longer period, in business days, that the Minister has specified under s 360P(11B); enter 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many business days does the provider have to answer` IS `the period to answer` `a longer period specified by the Minister`

@export If the provider refuses, how many business days can pass, at most, from the refusal until I must have a copy of the notice and the reasons (s 360P(12))?
GIVEN `business days between the provider's notice and my retailer receiving it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days after the provider gave the notice your retailer received it (0 if the same day)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How long until I must have the refusal reasons` IS
    `the business days to give written notice of a refusal` PLUS `business days between the provider's notice and my retailer receiving it` PLUS `the business days for my retailer to pass on the refusal notice`

§§ `s 360P(8), (9), s 360W -- on what terms I am connected`

-- s 360P(9): if the provider must connect and "the connection is not covered by an agreement between the statutory
-- infrastructure provider and the carriage service provider", it "must comply with the obligation on the terms and conditions
-- that were made available on the statutory infrastructure provider's website at the time when the request was made". (8): if
-- the retailer asks for an agreement on the same terms as those published, the provider "must comply with the request".
-- s 360W(2): the published terms "must include the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure provider must so
-- connect premises"; (4): they have "no effect to the extent to which" they are inconsistent with a s 360U standard or s 360V
-- rules. These are terms between the provider and the retailer; the end-user's own contract is with the retailer.
DECLARE `On what terms` IS ONE OF
    `the terms of the agreement between the provider and my retailer that covers the connection`
    `the terms the provider published on its website when the request was made, including the maximum connection period, except where they are inconsistent with a standard or rules (ss 360P(9), 360W(2), (4))`
    `an agreement on the published terms: my retailer asked for one, and the provider must enter it (s 360P(8))`

@export On what terms must the provider connect my premises?
GIVEN `an agreement between the provider and my retailer covers the connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider and your retailer have an agreement that covers this connection
      `my retailer asked for an agreement on the published terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your retailer has asked the provider to enter an agreement on the same terms the provider publishes on its website
GIVETH AN `On what terms`
DECIDE `On what terms question` IS
    IF `an agreement between the provider and my retailer covers the connection`
    THEN `the terms of the agreement between the provider and my retailer that covers the connection`
    ELSE IF `my retailer asked for an agreement on the published terms`
         THEN `an agreement on the published terms: my retailer asked for one, and the provider must enter it (s 360P(8))`
         ELSE `the terms the provider published on its website when the request was made, including the maximum connection period, except where they are inconsistent with a standard or rules (ss 360P(9), 360W(2), (4))`

§§ `s 360Q(1A), (1B) -- can I make voice calls on the service`

-- s 360Q(1A): "The eligible service must enable the carriage service provider to supply, to end-users at premises in the
-- service area, carriage services that can be used by those end-users to make and receive voice calls." (1B): "Subsection (1A)
-- does not apply if the carriage service is supplied using a satellite."
@export Must the provider's wholesale service let my retailer give me a service I can make and receive voice calls on?
GIVEN `my service is supplied using a satellite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service is supplied using a satellite
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the wholesale service support voice calls` IF NOT `my service is supplied using a satellite`

§§ `ss 360R, 360SA -- if my area's provider will no longer be able to serve it`

-- s 360R(1): applies to the provider "for: (a) a nominated service area; or (aa) an anticipated service area; or (b) a
-- designated service area" -- not to NBN Co for the general service area. (2): if it "becomes aware that it is likely that
-- [it] will no longer be able to fulfil [its] obligations under section 360P or 360Q", it must give written notice to the
-- Secretary, the ACMA and its customers "at least 12 months before" if reasonably practicable, otherwise "not later than 10
-- business days after"; (3) the same, 90 days ahead, if another carrier or carriage service provider is willing to take over.
-- s 360SA: a carriage service provider that receives such a notice, where "the matter is likely to result in a change to, or
-- the disruption of, qualifying carriage services provided by the carriage service provider to end-users", "must: (a) give
-- written notice of the matter to each of those end-users; and (b) do so within 5 business days after receiving the notice".
`the business days for my retailer to pass on a provider's notice` MEANS 5

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Telecom party` `Telecom act`
DECIDE `s 360SA(2) -- my retailer must tell me of the provider's notice within 5 business days` IS
    PARTY `my carriage service provider`
    MUST  `give me written notice of the matter`
    WITHIN `the business days for my retailer to pass on a provider's notice`
    LEST  BREACH BY `my carriage service provider` BECAUSE "s 360SA(2): the carriage service provider must give the end-user written notice of the matter within 5 business days after receiving the provider's notice"

DECLARE `Must I be told` IS ONE OF
    `yes: my retailer must give me written notice of the matter within 5 business days after it receives the provider's notice (s 360SA)`
    `no notice under Part 19: s 360R does not apply to NBN Co as the provider for the general service area`
    `no notice under s 360SA: it applies only where the matter is likely to change or disrupt the qualifying services my retailer provides me`
    `not yet: my retailer must tell me within 5 business days of receiving a notice under s 360R(2) or (3), and has not received one`

@export If the provider for my area is likely to stop being able to connect or serve it, must I be told, and by when?
GIVEN `my provider is NBN Co for the general service area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your statutory infrastructure provider is NBN Co for the general service area (TRUE), rather than the provider for a nominated, anticipated or designated service area
      `my retailer has received the provider's notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your retailer has received written notice from the provider under s 360R(2) or (3) that it is likely to stop being able to meet its obligations, or that another provider is willing to take over
      `the matter is likely to change or disrupt my service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter is likely to change or disrupt the broadband (qualifying carriage services) your retailer provides you
GIVETH A `Must I be told`
DECIDE `Must I be told question` IS
    IF `my provider is NBN Co for the general service area`
    THEN `no notice under Part 19: s 360R does not apply to NBN Co as the provider for the general service area`
    ELSE IF (NOT `the matter is likely to change or disrupt my service`)
         THEN `no notice under s 360SA: it applies only where the matter is likely to change or disrupt the qualifying services my retailer provides me`
         ELSE IF `my retailer has received the provider's notice`
              THEN `yes: my retailer must give me written notice of the matter within 5 business days after it receives the provider's notice (s 360SA)`
              ELSE `not yet: my retailer must tell me within 5 business days of receiving a notice under s 360R(2) or (3), and has not received one`

§§ `ss 360VD, 360VE -- if the provider breaches a designated compensable standard or rule`

-- s 360VD(1), (2): if a statutory infrastructure provider "contravenes a designated compensable standard" (or rule) and "the
-- contravention relates to a particular customer", it "is liable to pay damages to the customer for the contravention".
-- s 360VB: "customer includes prospective customer"; "damages includes punitive damages". (3): the amount is "ascertained in
-- accordance with the compensation rules" (not deposited: an input). (4): reduced "(but not below zero)" by a credit or payment
-- made under another right or remedy "aris[ing] out of the same event or transaction". (5): recoverable "by action against the
-- statutory infrastructure provider in a court of competent jurisdiction". (7): "An action under this section must be
-- instituted within 2 years after: (a) in the case of a contravention that continued throughout a period--the time when the
-- contravention began; or (b) in any other case--the time when the contravention occurred." Which standards or rules are
-- designated compensable is set by instruments not deposited; whether the contravention relates to me is asked as fact.
DECLARE `Can I claim damages` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the provider is liable to pay me damages for the contravention, in the amount the compensation rules give less what I have already been credited or paid for the same event (s 360VD)` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `no: s 360VD gives damages only for a contravention of a designated compensable standard or rule that relates to me as the provider's customer or prospective customer`

@export The provider broke a designated compensable standard or rule. Can I claim damages, and how much?
GIVEN `the provider contravened a designated compensable standard or rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider contravened a standard (s 360U) or rule (s 360V) that the Minister has declared a designated compensable standard or rule
      `the contravention relates to me as its customer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contravention relates to you as a customer (or prospective customer) of the provider
      `damages under the compensation rules` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages, in dollars, that the compensation rules (made under s 360VH) give for this contravention
      `already credited or paid for the same event` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars the provider has already credited or paid you for the same event under another right or remedy (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Can I claim damages`
DECIDE `Can I claim damages question` IS
    IF `the provider contravened a designated compensable standard or rule` AND `the contravention relates to me as its customer`
    THEN `yes: the provider is liable to pay me damages for the contravention, in the amount the compensation rules give less what I have already been credited or paid for the same event (s 360VD)` (max 0 (`damages under the compensation rules` MINUS `already credited or paid for the same event`))
    ELSE `no: s 360VD gives damages only for a contravention of a designated compensable standard or rule that relates to me as the provider's customer or prospective customer`

-- s 360VD(7): within 2 years after the contravention (or after it began). "2 years after" day N: by the same day 2 years later
-- (29 February to 28 February).
@export By when must I start a court action for damages under s 360VD?
GIVEN `the day the contravention occurred or began` IS A DATE @desc The day the contravention happened, or, if it went on over a period, the day it began
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I sue for damages` IS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day the contravention occurred or began` EQUALS 2 AND DATE_DAY `the day the contravention occurred or began` EQUALS 29
    THEN Date 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the day the contravention occurred or began` PLUS 2)
    ELSE Date (DATE_DAY `the day the contravention occurred or began`) (DATE_MONTH `the day the contravention occurred or began`) (DATE_YEAR `the day the contravention occurred or began` PLUS 2)

-- s 360VE(1): once the provider "first has reason to believe that an event has occurred that is reasonably likely to result in
-- [it] being liable to pay damages to a particular customer", it "must: (a) decide whether to accept that liability; and (b) do
-- so: (i) within 14 days after that time; or (ii)" a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule. (3): if it does
-- not accept, it "must give the customer written notification of the decision within 14 weeks after the decision is made".
-- (4), (5): if it accepts, "the liability must be discharged within the period of 14 weeks after the decision is made". In days.
`the days to decide whether to accept liability` MEANS 14
`the days to notify or discharge after deciding` MEANS 98

GIVEN `a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the days to decide` IS
    IF `a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule`
    ELSE `the days to decide whether to accept liability`

GIVEN `a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Telecom party` `Telecom act`
DECIDE `s 360VE -- the provider must decide on liability, then pay me or tell me it will not` IS
    PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider`
    MUST  `decide whether to accept liability for damages` decision
    WITHIN `the days to decide` `a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule`
    HENCE
        IF decision EQUALS `accepts the liability`
        THEN PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider`
             MUST  `discharge the liability`
             WITHIN `the days to notify or discharge after deciding`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the statutory infrastructure provider` BECAUSE "s 360VE(4), (5): an accepted liability must be discharged within 14 weeks after the decision"
        ELSE PARTY `the statutory infrastructure provider`
             MUST  `give me written notification that it does not accept liability`
             WITHIN `the days to notify or discharge after deciding`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the statutory infrastructure provider` BECAUSE "s 360VE(3): the provider must notify the customer in writing within 14 weeks after deciding not to accept liability"
    LEST  BREACH BY `the statutory infrastructure provider` BECAUSE "s 360VE(1): the provider must decide whether to accept the liability within 14 days (or the relevant number of days)"

@export Once the provider has reason to believe it may owe me damages, how many days, at most, until it must have paid me or told me in writing that it will not?
GIVEN `a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule` IS A NUMBER @desc A number of days declared for the particular standard or rule under s 360U(3C) or s 360V(1C) to decide on liability; enter 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days until the provider must pay or refuse` IS
    `the days to decide` `a relevant number of days declared for the standard or rule` PLUS `the days to notify or discharge after deciding`
